  "id": "COMPOUND:29957 - PROTEIN:6151",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a complex but consistent relationship between 4'-O-methylmelanettin and Ataxin-2, mediated through H(+)/Cl(-) exchange transporter 3. This transporter is identified as a target of multiple compounds, including 2,4-Bis[(4-hydroxyphenyl)methyl]-5-methoxy-3-[2-(3-methoxyphenyl)ethyl]phenol and (2E,4E)-N-isobutylundeca-2,4-dien-8,10-diynamide, all of which have a target of Ataxin-2. The shared target of these compounds, H(+)/Cl(-) exchange transporter 3, indicates a potential mechanism by which 4'-O-methylmelanettin may influence Ataxin-2 function. The evidence suggests that 4'-O-methylmelanettin may act as a modulator of this transporter, potentially affecting Ataxin-2 activity. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role for 4'-O-methylmelanettin in regulating Ataxin-2 through a transporter-dependent mechanism, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
